    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d445-a1-a2">

                <pb facs="0610" n="504" xml:id="pg504"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure B.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Col. Lindhamer to
                        Consul Black</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nuremberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-01-27"><hi rendition="#italic">January 27,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Answered briefly by the respectful statement that Johann Haberacker (typesetter),
                    born at Windsheim, has on August 5, 1890, been mustered into the regiment (owing
                    military duty), who might not otherwise be found for service when wanted (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">unsicherer Dienstpflichtiger</hi>).</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lindhamer</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Colonel Fourteenth Infantry
                    Regiment</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
